## The one still OPEN, and what would settle it

**#471 — the shard lock's waiting policy under OVERSUBSCRIPTION.** Its records
are landed; its code is not. It is NOT a duplicate of #504:

  #504     4 arms, `c256x2048`, **t=8**, n=15 -> all inside a +/-1.8% floor.
           Its own not-measured list ends with `t=16`
           (`benchmarks/c256_contention_2026-08-11.meta:128`).
  #471     spin-64-then-yield, `v4k_8tile{,_10b}`, t=1..16, n=16, IDLE box,
           `foreign_max = 0` on every committed row
           -> null at t=1/2/4/8 (agrees with #504)
           -> **0.955 (8bpc) / 0.960 (10bpc) at t=16**, p90 and max moving by
              the same factor.

t=16 is the only cell on this host where threads (16) exceed cores (12 logical).
The shipping build spins unbounded — `yield_now` lived only behind a probe
feature that #504's arms have since replaced.

Settles it: the **t=12 / t=24 / t=32 ladder** (queued on #471, never got an idle
window) and **x86_64**, where `spin_loop()` is `pause` and the scheduler is not
heterogeneous, so nothing here transfers. Do not re-litigate at t <= 8; that is
now null on two cells and two vectors.

